# P3 · AI-drafted notes under clinician review · Weeks 13–20 · R3 Scribe
# exit: 1 0 fabricated medicines/doses across eval set · 2 ≥ 80 % drafts signed with minor edits · 3 consent for 100 % of recordings; declined path tested · 4 trust survey + note time vs P2 baseline
# nfr:  1 draft ≤ 60 s p50 after stop · 2 no training on customer data without separate lawful basis · 3 AI vendor DPA + regional processing confirmed per country
# pkg:  1 AI safety card · 2 waiting-room consent notice EN/HI/AR · 3 evaluation report + AI incident procedure
# dep:  1 Azure OpenAI / Speech availability Central India & UAE North · 2 legal review of recording consent per market

@epic MDV-P3-E01 | Recording consent and policy | P3-01 | Per-encounter consent separate from treatment consent; decline and revocation always safe.
@epic MDV-P3-E02 | Capture and upload | P3-02 | Phone or desktop capture with visible state and resilient encrypted upload.
@epic MDV-P3-E03 | Transcription, speakers and AI worker | P3-03, P3-07 | In-region transcription with provisional speakers, via an unprivileged .NET AI worker.
@epic MDV-P3-E04 | Evidence-linked draft and review | P3-04, P3-05, P3-08 | Every drafted statement links to its source; the doctor accepts, edits and signs.
@epic MDV-P3-E05 | Safety states | P3-06 | Emergency prompt, AI outage, wrong patient and overlap handled without data loss or autonomy.
@epic MDV-P3-E06 | AI quality, compliance and R3 gate | P3-07 | Evaluation in CI, vendor/legal clearance, safety materials and the R3 gate.

=== MDV-P3-001
title: Spike: Azure AI Speech and Azure OpenAI in-region capability check and ADR for speech/LLM providers
type: Spike
epic: MDV-P3-E06
prd: P3-07, P3-03
covers: dep:1
priority: MUST
roles: Developer
labels: ai, spike, adr
estimate: 2
weeks: 13
depends: MDV-P0-003
confidence: 70 | Regional model availability and Tamil/Hindi diarisation quality are unknown until tested.
sources: PRD v2 P3 dependency 1, risk "AI model not available in-region"; docs/03-architecture/ai-pipeline.md
desc:
In the launch region confirm: batch transcription with diarisation and language identification for en-IN, hi-IN, ta-IN (and ar-AE for UAE), Azure OpenAI chat model with JSON-schema output, data residency/processing terms. Run 10 synthetic recordings through the pipeline and measure WER, diarisation error and latency. Record ADR-007 (speech/LLM providers, models, versions, regions, fallback).
ac:
- ADR-007 accepted with model names/versions, regions, quotas and fallback provider abstraction.
- Measured latency supports the ≤ 60 s p50 draft target or the gap is quantified with a plan.
- Language/diarisation quality per language is recorded on the synthetic set.
- Confirmation that no data leaves the country for inference (documented with Microsoft terms).

=== MDV-P3-002
title: Consent templates and recording policy administration (H-09)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P3-E01
prd: P3-01
screens: H-09
priority: MUST
roles: Practice admin
labels: consent, admin
estimate: 2
weeks: 13
depends: MDV-P1-019
confidence: 82 | Wireframe defines templates per language, kinds, retention and versioning.
sources: design/Medvya Wireframes (H-09); docs/04-security-compliance/README.md#consent-model-separate-versioned-receipts
desc:
/admin/consent: consent templates per kind (treatment, recording, sharing, reminders, marketing) and language (EN/TA/HI/AR…) with versions (e.g. v2026.2); recording policy (audio retention days and purpose, who may record, devices allowed). Publishing a new version never changes old receipts.
ac:
- Admin can draft, preview and publish a template version per language; published versions are immutable.
- Receipts reference the exact template version and language shown.
- Recording policy (retention days default 30, purpose "documentation only") is editable only by admins and audited.
- Recording consent script in the patient's language is served from the published template.

=== MDV-P3-003
title: Per-encounter recording consent with device selection; decline goes straight to manual note (A-02, E-04)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P3-E01
prd: P3-01
screens: A-02
covers: exit:3
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: consent, capture
estimate: 3
weeks: 13-14
depends: MDV-P3-002, MDV-P2-009
confidence: 86 | Hi-fi consent screen with script languages, pill states and device list.
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (A-02); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#ai-scribe-p3--medvya-clinician-app-medvya-clinical-screens
desc:
Encounter step "Consent": show consent script in the chosen language (English/Tamil/Hindi; Arabic for UAE) for the doctor to read; record decision given/declined, by whom (patient, guardian), people in the room (ENCOUNTER_PARTICIPANT), device choice (this phone with mic test, desk microphone, clip disabled until P6). Decline → manual note (E-04) with "No recording for this visit. You can write the note manually." and no guilt copy. Consent pill in the banner.
ac:
- Recording cannot start without a "given" consent receipt for this encounter (server-enforced; FSM CONSENT_VERIFIED).
- 100 % of recording sessions reference a consent receipt (database constraint + test; exit gate 3).
- Declined path leads to the manual note with the same sign flow (Playwright test).
- Consent is per encounter; treatment consent at registration never implies recording consent.
- Microphone permission denial shows guidance and offers manual note.

=== MDV-P3-004
title: Consent revoked mid-visit stops capture and discards later audio (A-09)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P3-E01
prd: P3-01
screens: A-09
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: consent, safety
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 15
depends: MDV-P3-005
confidence: 88 | Designed state with copy and receipt.
sources: design/Medvya Clinical Screens (A-09b Consent withdrawn); docs/03-architecture/state-machines.md#capture-fsm-p3-p6
desc:
"Patient withdrew consent" action during recording: capture stops immediately (CONSENT_REVOKED), audio after the revocation time is discarded client- and server-side, pending AI jobs are cancelled or limited to pre-revocation audio per policy, a receipt is recorded, and the doctor continues manually.
ac:
- After revocation no further chunks are accepted for that session (server rejects).
- Audio after the revocation timestamp is deleted and the deletion is recorded.
- Pending jobs re-check consent and do not process revoked ranges (worker test).
- UI shows "Recording stopped at {t}. Audio after withdrawal was discarded." and a "Continue manually" action.

=== MDV-P3-005
title: Capture on phone (mobile web) or desktop mic with timer, pause, consent indicator and warnings (A-03, X-01)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P3-E02
prd: P3-02
screens: A-03, X-01
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: capture, audio, mobile
estimate: 3
weeks: 14-15
depends: MDV-P3-003
confidence: 80 | Designed; iOS Safari background/lock-screen audio limits need testing.
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (A-03); design/Medvya Mobile and Tablet (Capture · recording)
desc:
MediaRecorder capture in browser: large REC timer, pause/resume, stop, waveform (static with reduced motion), consent pill always visible, live provisional transcript panel (if supported, marked provisional, never auto-entering the record). Mobile: screen stays awake (Wake Lock), lock-screen/notification shows recording indicator without PHI. Battery and network warnings. Low audio warning (A-06d) if levels too low.
ac:
- Start/pause/stop transitions follow the capture FSM and are mirrored server-side.
- The recording indicator and timer are visible at all times during capture, including on mobile.
- No PHI appears in OS notifications or the page title while recording.
- Warnings appear for battery < 20 %, offline/poor network and low audio level, each with text guidance.
- Works on current Chrome/Edge desktop, Android Chrome and iOS Safari (tested matrix recorded).

=== MDV-P3-006
title: Encrypted chunked upload with resume; upload progress, failed/partial recovery states (A-06)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P3-E02
prd: P3-02
screens: A-06
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: upload, resilience
estimate: 3
weeks: 15
depends: MDV-P3-005
confidence: 82 | States designed (A-06a/b); resumable upload pattern known.
sources: design/Medvya Clinical Screens (A-06a, A-06b); docs/03-architecture/ai-pipeline.md
desc:
Audio split into sequence-numbered chunks, encrypted in transit, uploaded with a user-delegation SAS scoped to one session prefix; chunk manifest with SHA-256 committed via API. Interrupted transfer resumes only missing chunks (TRANSFER_INTERRUPTED). States: "Uploading 14 of 17 encrypted chunks" (review can start), "Upload failed · 3 chunks missing" with recovered range and options Retry from phone / Continue partial (missing range flagged in transcript and draft).
ac:
- Killing the network mid-upload and restoring resumes without re-sending committed chunks and without duplicates (test).
- A SAS token cannot write outside its session prefix and expires within minutes.
- Integrity hash mismatch rejects a chunk and requests re-upload.
- Continuing with partial audio marks the missing time range in the transcript and every affected draft section.
- No audio is retained on the device after successful upload (cleared buffer).

=== MDV-P3-007
title: Azure Service Bus and .NET AI worker skeleton without database credentials (scoped job + callback)
type: Task
epic: MDV-P3-E03
prd: P3-07
priority: MUST
roles: Developer
labels: ai-worker, service-bus, security
estimate: 3
weeks: 14-15
depends: MDV-P3-001
confidence: 85 | Architecture specified in PRD v2 P3-07 and the AI pipeline doc.
sources: PRD v2 P3-07; docs/03-architecture/ai-pipeline.md#worker-privileges
desc:
Service Bus namespace (private endpoint) and queues with dead-letter; outbox dispatcher publishes opaque job ids; Worker.Ai (.NET 10, Microsoft.Extensions.AI) authenticates with its own managed identity, calls a restricted internal API to re-check consent/tenant/retention and obtain short-lived audio access, and returns results through an authenticated internal callback. Prompts and model versions are versioned files in the repo.
ac:
- The worker identity has no database permissions (verified in infra test) and cannot call public endpoints beyond the internal API.
- Duplicate delivery of the same job produces exactly one logical result (idempotency test).
- Poison messages go to dead-letter with an alert; no PHI in message bodies.
- Each AI run records model ref, prompt hash, schema version and region.

=== MDV-P3-008
title: Transcription with diarisation and language identification (in-region Azure AI Speech)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P3-E03
prd: P3-03
covers: nfr:1
priority: MUST
roles: System
labels: transcription, ai
estimate: 3
weeks: 15-16
depends: MDV-P3-007, MDV-P3-006
confidence: 75 | Mixed Tamil/Hindi/English quality is unproven until the spike and evaluation results.
sources: PRD v2 P3-03; design/Medvya Clinician App (SEGS sample: Tamil/Hindi/English)
desc:
Batch transcription of the completed recording (authoritative source), diarisation into provisional speakers, per-segment language and original-language text with English translation, timestamps and confidence bands. TRANSCRIPT, TRANSCRIPT_SEGMENT (encrypted content), SPEAKER_LABEL (provisional). Provisional live captions never populate the record.
ac:
- A 10-minute synthetic consultation is transcribed and diarised with segments, timestamps, language tags and translations.
- Segment content is stored encrypted; no transcript text appears in logs/telemetry.
- Transcription latency contributes ≤ 40 s p50 for a 10-minute visit, leaving budget for drafting (overall ≤ 60 s p50 measured in MDV-P3-025).
- Low-confidence segments are marked and surfaced in review.

=== MDV-P3-009
title: Multi-speaker transcript review with speaker confirmation (A-04)
type: Story
